@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dct:  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xeo:  <https://xeoontology.org/xeo#> .

# XEO Design module: what a website is designed and built with, and how a new
# design is proposed, shown and decided.
#
# DRAFT, new in 0.8. Every term here carries xeo:termStatus "draft": declared so it
# can be tried against real data, and free to change or go without a deprecation
# step. A class stays draft until an example file loads it and its maintainer
# lifts the mark. examples/design-review.jsonld loads all ten classes, and
# tools/validate.py says so in a note. docs/design/research-prompt.md is the
# prompt for checking these terms against the design tools' own vocabularies.
#
# TWO HALVES.
#
#   What a site is built with (durable, the design system):
#     DesignSystem - the tokens, components, patterns and templates (inDesignSystem)
#     DesignToken  - aliasOf -> DesignToken ; tokenType, tokenValue, tokenTier, tokenMode
#     DesignComponent - variantOf -> DesignComponent ; variantValue ; usesToken, composedOf, usesAsset
#     DesignPattern   - composedOf -> DesignComponent | DesignPattern
#     PageTemplate    - composedOf -> DesignComponent | DesignPattern
#     DesignAsset     - a file: logo, icon, image, font (assetKind)
#     designRecordRef - on any of these: the tool's own id for the record
#     Website - usesDesignSystem -> DesignSystem ;  URL - usesTemplate -> PageTemplate
#
#   How a new design is proposed and decided (the review):
#     DesignDirection - directionFor -> Website | Brand | Project ; proposedIn -> Deliverable
#     DesignElement   - elementOf -> Website ; seenOn -> URL   (the existing site's parts)
#     DesignConcept   - depicts -> component | pattern | template | element | URL
#                       underDirection -> DesignDirection ; replacesElement -> DesignElement
#     DesignDecision  - decidesOn -> element | direction | concept ; designVerdict
#                       underDirection, chosenConcept, decidedBy -> Person
#     DesignSystem - fromDirection -> DesignDirection   (the system built from the pick)
#
# EACH THING HAS ITS LAYER. Everything in a design system, and every direction,
# element and concept, is an entity: a durable thing other records point at. The
# one interpretation is the DesignDecision, a reviewer's judgment of fit. A
# direction carries no "approved" flag: approval is a decision about it, kept
# with who made it and when, so a later change of mind does not overwrite it.
#
# TOKENS FOLLOW THE W3C DESIGN TOKENS FORMAT. A token's name is its path in the
# token file, its type one of that format's types (xeos:tokenType), and an alias
# is a token pointing at another. Modes (light and dark, one brand and another)
# are one token per mode. Checked on 2026-11-20 against the format's Resolver
# Module 2025.10: a mode there is a context of a modifier, each context its own
# set of token files merged by path, so one value per token per context; Adobe
# Spectrum's design data likewise keeps one row per mode
# (docs/design/research-results-2026-11-20.md). A value that depends on more than
# one axis (dark and mobile) is one token per combination, with one tokenMode per
# axis, each written modifier:context (theme:dark, scale:mobile).
#
# POINTERS, NEVER FILES. A design file, a component library, a mockup and an
# image stay where they are made and kept; the graph holds where (artifactUri,
# core) and how they relate. A tool's own identifier for a record (a Figma
# variable key, a Canva design id) is its designRecordRef, the join back to the
# tool. How a tool's fields map to these terms belongs in a mapping file.
#
# SETTLED FOR 0.8, from the nine questions the check against the design tools
# left open (docs/design/research-results-2026-11-20.md, section 6). Three are
# terms: a mode on more than one axis is several tokenMode values; what makes a
# variant is its variantValue; a tool's own id is a designRecordRef. The verdict
# revise stays. Four are deliberately not terms here. A site's copy tone (voice)
# is the brand's, not an elementKind. A direction's rank within its proposal is
# a judgment, kept as DesignDecisions (shortlist, reject) with a statement. A
# handoff state (ready for development, completed) is a state of the build
# work, which belongs with the WorkItem (work), not a designVerdict. The rights
# to an asset (licence, credit, expiry) wait until a project needs them, and
# will then follow schema.org. And accessibility check results (contrast,
# alternative text) are planned as a draft observation class for 0.9.
#
# NOT HERE YET, and each an open question: breakpoints and responsive rules; a
# CMS block as a kind of component; the atomic-design levels (atom, molecule,
# organism) as a scheme; and a design file's pages and frames.
#
# NEEDS core only (Website, URL, Person, name, artifactUri, occurredAt). Points
# at Brand (visibility), Project and Deliverable (work) and statement (decision)
# where those are loaded; each such link is optional.
#
# Sources: the W3C Design Tokens Community Group's Design Tokens Format Module
# 2025.10 for token types and aliases, and its Resolver Module 2025.10 for modes;
# Figma's documentation of variables, modes,
# components and variants, as read on 2026-11-20; atomic design (Frost, 2016) for
# the ladder from component to pattern to template; and the working practice of
# a design proposal reviewed element by element. Names here are ours unless the
# line says otherwise.

xeo:design-module a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "XEO Design (design systems, tokens, components, patterns, templates, assets, directions, concepts, review decisions)" ;
    dct:description "Draft. What a website is designed and built with: a DesignSystem of tokens, components, patterns and page templates, and the assets they use; and how a new design is proposed and decided: DesignDirections, the existing site's DesignElements, DesignConcepts drawn under a direction, and the reviewer's DesignDecisions to keep, replace or approve. Holds pointers, never files. Needs only core. Every term is marked draft." ;
    dct:creator "Inbound Found" ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.8.1" .

# --- The design system -------------------------------------------------------------

xeo:DesignSystem a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Design System" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A named, versioned set of the decisions a brand's or a site's interfaces are built from: its tokens, components, patterns and page templates (each inDesignSystem), and the assets they use. Identified by name and designSystemVersion. Kept where it is maintained, a design file, a code library or a documentation site (artifactUri, core): the graph holds the pointer and the structure, never the files. A Website is built with one (usesDesignSystem). One built out of a proposed direction names it (fromDirection)." .

xeo:DesignToken a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Design Token" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "One named design decision stored as a value, so design files and code share it: a colour, a spacing step, a font family, a duration, a shadow. Its name (core) is its path in the token file, such as color.brand.primary; its tokenType is one of the W3C Design Tokens Format's types; its tokenValue is the value as written there. A token that refers to another (an alias, {color.blue.500} in that format) names it with aliasOf and need carry no value of its own. tokenTier says whether it is a primitive, a semantic or a component token. A token whose value changes by mode (light and dark, one brand and another; Figma calls these modes) is one token per mode, each with its tokenMode; where the value depends on more than one axis (dark and mobile), one token per combination, with one tokenMode per axis. Belongs to one DesignSystem." .

xeo:DesignComponent a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Design Component" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A reusable piece of interface with a name and a defined anatomy: a button, a card, a header, a form field. Built from tokens (usesToken), smaller components (composedOf) and assets (usesAsset). A variant (the primary button of a button, the compact card of a card) is a component of its own that points at the one it varies (variantOf) and says what sets it apart (variantValue). Kept where it is defined, a design file or a code library (artifactUri, core); the component in the design file and the one in code are one DesignComponent where they are meant to match. Not an HTML element, and not a CMS block, though a block may implement one." .

xeo:DesignPattern a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Design Pattern" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A reusable answer to a recurring interface problem, made of components: a hero, a pricing table, a filtered listing, a sign-up flow. Larger than a component and smaller than a page; composedOf names the components and patterns it is made of. A pattern says how a problem is solved. Whether a page must use it is a Practice (decision), not a property of the pattern." .

xeo:PageTemplate a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Page Template" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The layout a kind of page is built from, and the patterns and components it holds (composedOf): the template for a home page, a service page, an article, a case study. Many URLs use one (usesTemplate). Not a page role (hasRole, decision), which is a reading of what a page is for: a template is what the page is built from, as the CMS or the build records it." .

xeo:DesignAsset a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Design Asset" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A file a design uses: a logo, an icon, an illustration, a photograph, a graphic, a font, a video (assetKind). Identified by where the file is kept (artifactUri, core); the graph holds the pointer, never the file. Used by components, patterns, templates, concepts and pages (usesAsset). Who may use it, and on what terms (licence, credit, expiry), is not a term yet: it waits until a project needs it, and will then follow schema.org." .

xeo:inDesignSystem a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "in design system" ;
    xeo:domainIncludes xeo:DesignToken , xeo:DesignComponent , xeo:DesignPattern , xeo:PageTemplate , xeo:DesignAsset ;
    rdfs:range xeo:DesignSystem ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The DesignSystem a token, component, pattern, template or asset belongs to. One per token; a component or an asset shared by two systems may name both. Domain left open across the terms listed." .

xeo:usesDesignSystem a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "uses design system" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Website ; rdfs:range xeo:DesignSystem ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The DesignSystem a Website's pages are built with. A site moving to a new system keeps both links, each with startedAt and endedAt where the dates are known." .

xeo:aliasOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "alias of" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignToken ; rdfs:range xeo:DesignToken ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The token whose value this token takes: a semantic token such as color.action.primary pointing at a primitive such as color.blue.500. At most one. A chain of aliases is followed to the token that holds the value; a loop is an error. The Design Tokens Format's alias, written {group.token} there, or a $ref JSON Pointer to the whole token. A reference to one part of a composite value ($ref into a shadow's colour, say) is not an alias: it stays inside the tokenValue as written." .

xeo:usesToken a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "uses token" ;
    xeo:domainIncludes xeo:DesignComponent , xeo:DesignPattern , xeo:PageTemplate , xeo:DesignConcept ;
    rdfs:range xeo:DesignToken ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A DesignToken a component, pattern, template or concept is styled with. Says which decisions it depends on, so a token's change can be traced to everything it touches. Domain left open across the terms listed." .

xeo:composedOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "composed of" ;
    xeo:domainIncludes xeo:DesignComponent , xeo:DesignPattern , xeo:PageTemplate ;
    xeo:rangeIncludes xeo:DesignComponent , xeo:DesignPattern ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A component or pattern this one is built from: a card from a heading, an image and a button; a hero from a heading and a call to action; a template from its patterns. Order and slots are not modelled. Domain and range left open across the terms listed." .

xeo:variantOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "variant of" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignComponent ; rdfs:range xeo:DesignComponent ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The component this one is a variant of: the primary button of a button, the compact card of a card. What makes it a variant (size, state, emphasis) is its variantValue. Figma's variant within a component set: there each variant is a component inside the set, so the variant points at the DesignComponent that stands for the set. Penpot's variants are the same shape. Adobe Spectrum uses the word variant for one option of a component (accent, primary), not for a component of its own." .

xeo:usesAsset a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "uses asset" ;
    xeo:domainIncludes xeo:DesignComponent , xeo:DesignPattern , xeo:PageTemplate , xeo:DesignConcept , xeo:URL ;
    rdfs:range xeo:DesignAsset ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A DesignAsset shown or loaded by a component, pattern, template, concept or page: the logo in a header, the photograph on a page, the font a template loads. Domain left open across the terms listed." .

xeo:usesTemplate a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "uses template" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:URL ; rdfs:range xeo:PageTemplate ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The PageTemplate a page is built from, as the CMS or the build records it. One per page at a time. A template inferred from a crawl, by comparing layouts, is a reading and carries method." .

xeo:designSystemVersion a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "design system version" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignSystem ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The version of a DesignSystem as its maintainers name it, such as 3.2.0. A new version is the same DesignSystem with a new value, or a new node where both versions are in use at once." .

xeo:tokenType a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "token type" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignToken ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "What kind of value a DesignToken holds, as one of the W3C Design Tokens Format's type names: color, dimension, fontFamily, fontWeight, duration, cubicBezier, number, and the composite strokeStyle, border, transition, shadow, gradient and typography. Two more, string and boolean, are not in that format and cover Figma's variables of those types (and Tokens Studio's text and boolean tokens). Codes in xeos:tokenType, spelled as the format spells them. Exactly one per token: where the file sets the type on a group, or leaves an alias to take its target's type, the type the format resolves to." .

xeo:tokenValue a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "token value" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignToken ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A DesignToken's value as written in its token file, as text. Where the file writes a JSON object or array, the JSON: in the Design Tokens Format 2025.10 a colour ({\"colorSpace\": \"srgb\", \"components\": [0.1, 0.45, 0.91], \"hex\": \"#1a73e8\"}), a dimension ({\"value\": 16, \"unit\": \"px\"}), a duration ({\"value\": 200, \"unit\": \"ms\"}) and every composite (a shadow, a typography style) are objects. A file in an older or a tool's own format may write #1a73e8, 16px or 200ms, stored as written. Absent on an alias, which takes its value from the token it names (aliasOf)." .

xeo:tokenTier a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "token tier" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignToken ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "Which tier of a design system a DesignToken sits in: primitive (a raw value with no meaning of its own, such as blue.500), semantic (a value named for its use, such as color.action.primary, usually an alias of a primitive) or component (a value for one component, such as button.background). Codes in xeos:tokenTier. Systems name the tiers differently: Material Design 3 says reference, system and component; the Design Tokens Format's Color Module, in a non-normative note, base, alias and component; Adobe Spectrum primitive (also global), semantic and component, its own spelling of these three codes. The Design Tokens Format itself defines no tiers." .

xeo:tokenMode a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "token mode" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignToken ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The mode a DesignToken's value holds in, where the system has more than one: light or dark, one brand or another, compact or comfortable. A token with a value per mode is one DesignToken per mode, each with the same name and its tokenMode. Where the system has one axis of modes, the mode as the system names it (dark). Where a value depends on more than one axis (dark and mobile), one tokenMode per axis, each written modifier:context (theme:dark, scale:mobile), and one DesignToken per combination that has a value of its own; a token carrying more than one tokenMode writes every one that way. The Design Tokens Format's Resolver Module calls a mode a context of a modifier (the dark context of a theme modifier), and the contexts of its modifiers multiply; Adobe Spectrum keeps mode sets for colour scheme, scale and contrast; Figma, a mode of a variable collection, one collection per axis. Free text, named as the system names its modifiers and modes. Absent where the system has one mode." .

xeo:assetKind a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "asset kind" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignAsset ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "What kind of file a DesignAsset is: logo, icon, illustration, photograph, graphic (a made image such as a banner or a social post), font, video or animation. Codes in xeos:assetKind. One per asset." .

xeo:variantValue a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "variant value" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignComponent ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "One property, and the value of it, that sets a variant apart from the component it varies, written property=value: size=small, state=hover, emphasis=quiet. One per axis, so a small quiet button carries two. A state (hover, pressed, disabled) is written the same way, as Figma and Penpot model states. The property names are the design system's own and are not a fixed list, because systems differ in their axes. Figma's variant properties in a component set, Penpot's variant properties, Adobe Spectrum's options and states, and the args of a Storybook story. Sits on a component that has a variantOf; absent on the component that stands for the whole set." .

xeo:designRecordRef a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "design record reference" ;
    xeo:domainIncludes xeo:DesignSystem , xeo:DesignToken , xeo:DesignComponent , xeo:DesignPattern , xeo:PageTemplate , xeo:DesignAsset , xeo:DesignConcept ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "Identity key of one record in the design tool that holds it, written tool:file:objectType:id (figma:<file key>:variable:<variable key>, canva:<design id>:page:<page id>). Two refs are the same record when all four parts match. The join back to the tool for a thing that has no address of its own: a variable or a token has no URL, so artifactUri cannot hold it. The file part is whatever the tool scopes the id to: a Figma file, a Canva design, a Creative Cloud library; a record the tool scopes to the account alone (a Canva asset) leaves that part empty and keeps its colon. One per tool the record is kept in, so a component kept in a design file and in a code library may carry two. Modelled on crmRecordRef (sales): the graph holds the pointer and never mirrors the tool's own schema. Which of a tool's identifiers is stable enough to use is said in its mapping file. Domain left open across the terms listed." .

# --- Proposing and deciding a design ---------------------------------------------

xeo:DesignDirection a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Design Direction" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "One proposed visual approach for a site or a brand: a name, the idea behind it in words (statement, decision), and how it treats type, colour, imagery and layout, shown through the DesignConcepts drawn under it (underDirection). Several are usually proposed together, in one Deliverable (proposedIn, work), for one Website, Brand or Project (directionFor). A durable option that concepts and decisions point at. Whether it fits is a reviewer's call, kept as a DesignDecision about it, never as a flag on the direction. Its rank among the directions of a proposal is not a property either: a ranking is a judgment, kept as the DesignDecisions about each direction (shortlist, reject) with a statement. A design system built out of a chosen direction names it (fromDirection)." .

xeo:DesignElement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Design Element" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "One part of an existing site's design, catalogued so it can be reviewed: a logo treatment, a colour, a type style, a style of photography, a divider, the navigation, a recurring component (elementKind). Belongs to one Website (elementOf) and is seen on its pages (seenOn). Where the same thing is also catalogued in a design system, realizedAs names the token, component, pattern, template or asset. A redesign asks of each element whether to keep, replace or remove it, and under each direction with what: a DesignDecision, and the DesignConcepts that replace it (replacesElement)." .

xeo:DesignConcept a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Design Concept" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A rendered proposal for one piece of interface, usually under one DesignDirection: a card, a hero, a page, or a direction's version of an element of the existing site. Names what it depicts (depicts: a component, pattern, template, element or page) and the direction it was drawn under (underDirection); where it is offered in place of an element of the existing site, replacesElement names that element. Kept as an image, a design-file frame or a prototype (artifactUri, core); the tool's own id for that frame or page is its designRecordRef. Where a model drew it, method and producedByModel (core) say how. A card concept is a DesignConcept that depicts a card component. Not a skos:Concept, which is a code in a scheme." .

xeo:DesignDecision a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Design Decision" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A reviewer's call on one piece of a design proposal: keep, replace or remove an element of the existing site; approve, shortlist, send back for changes (revise) or reject a direction or a concept; or defer (designVerdict). Names what it decides on (decidesOn), who decided (decidedBy), when (occurredAt, core), and, where the call holds under one direction only, which (underDirection). A replacement may name the concept chosen (chosenConcept). The reviewer's reason in their own words is its statement (decision). An interpretation: a judgment of fit, labeled as one. A changed mind is a new decision beside the old one, never an edit of it. Not Feedback (decision), which judges a machine's claim about a gap or a recommendation." .

xeo:directionFor a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "direction for" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignDirection ;
    xeo:rangeIncludes xeo:Website , xeo:Brand , xeo:Project ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "What a DesignDirection is proposed for: a Website, a Brand (visibility) or a Project (work), such as a new site that has no address yet. Range left open across the terms listed." .

xeo:proposedIn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "proposed in" ;
    xeo:domainIncludes xeo:DesignDirection , xeo:DesignConcept ;
    xeo:rangeIncludes xeo:Deliverable ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The Deliverable (work) a direction or a concept was handed over in: a proposal document, a proposal site, a review page. One deliverable usually holds several directions. Domain and range left open." .

xeo:elementOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "element of" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignElement ; rdfs:range xeo:Website ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The Website a DesignElement is part of. Exactly one per element." .

xeo:seenOn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "seen on" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignElement ; rdfs:range xeo:URL ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "A page where a DesignElement appears, as catalogued for review: an example, not a complete list. An element that is on every page names one or two." .

xeo:realizedAs a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "realized as" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignElement ;
    xeo:rangeIncludes xeo:DesignToken , xeo:DesignComponent , xeo:DesignPattern , xeo:PageTemplate , xeo:DesignAsset ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The design-system part an element of the existing site is: the colour token, the header component, the logo file. Absent where the site has no catalogued system, which is common on an older site. Range left open across the terms listed." .

xeo:depicts a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "depicts" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignConcept ;
    xeo:rangeIncludes xeo:DesignComponent , xeo:DesignPattern , xeo:PageTemplate , xeo:DesignElement , xeo:URL ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "What a DesignConcept shows: a component (a card), a pattern (a hero), a template (an article page), an element of the existing site, or one page (a URL). At least one per concept. Range left open across the terms listed." .

xeo:underDirection a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "under direction" ;
    xeo:domainIncludes xeo:DesignConcept , xeo:DesignDecision ;
    rdfs:range xeo:DesignDirection ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The DesignDirection a concept was drawn under, or a decision holds under: 'replace the divider, under direction three, with this'. At most one. A decision with none holds whichever direction is chosen. Domain left open across the terms listed." .

xeo:replacesElement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "replaces element" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignConcept ; rdfs:range xeo:DesignElement ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The element of the existing site a DesignConcept is offered in place of: one replacement option. Each direction may offer its own; the reviewer picks one with chosenConcept." .

xeo:fromDirection a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "from direction" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignSystem ; rdfs:range xeo:DesignDirection ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The DesignDirection a DesignSystem was built out of, once a direction was chosen. Absent on a system that came first." .

xeo:elementKind a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "element kind" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignElement ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "What kind of part of a design a DesignElement is: logo, color, typography, imagery, iconography, illustration, layout, navigation, component, pattern or motion. Codes in xeos:elementKind. One per element; something that is two kinds is catalogued as two elements. Copy tone (a brand's voice) is not a kind: the element review is visual, and voice belongs with the Brand (visibility)." .

xeo:decidesOn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "decides on" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignDecision ;
    xeo:rangeIncludes xeo:DesignElement , xeo:DesignDirection , xeo:DesignConcept ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "What a DesignDecision is about: an element of the existing site, a direction, or a concept. Exactly one per decision. Range left open across the terms listed." .

xeo:chosenConcept a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "chosen concept" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignDecision ; rdfs:range xeo:DesignConcept ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The concept a reviewer picked to replace an element, on a decision whose verdict is replace. Absent where the reviewer said replace and left the choice open." .

xeo:decidedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "decided by" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignDecision ; rdfs:range xeo:Person ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The Person (core) who made a DesignDecision: the client's reviewer, the designer, the team lead. Several where a group decided together." .

xeo:designVerdict a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "design verdict" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:DesignDecision ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    xeo:termStatus "draft" ;
    dct:description "The call a DesignDecision makes: keep, replace or remove (for an element of the existing site), approve, shortlist, revise or reject (for a direction or a concept), or defer (for any of them). revise is the changes-requested call design tools name: Figma's Request changes in a branch review, Canva's Needs changes in a design approval. A handoff state (ready for development, completed) is not a verdict: it is a state of the build work, which belongs with the WorkItem (work), not a call on fit. Codes in xeos:designVerdict. Exactly one per decision." .

# --- Terms from elsewhere, used here ----------------------------------------------
# New triples about terms declared in other modules; nothing is redefined.

xeo:artifactUri xeo:domainIncludes xeo:DesignSystem , xeo:DesignComponent , xeo:DesignPattern , xeo:PageTemplate , xeo:DesignAsset , xeo:DesignConcept .

xeo:statement xeo:domainIncludes xeo:DesignDirection , xeo:DesignDecision .
